\subsection{Instrumented Memory Handlers}

When logging is enabled, memory writes to Work RAM, VRAM, and Color RAM
are intercepted to record events. The original handlers in
[[setup\_berzerk\_memory]] are called first; the logger records the write
after the fact.

Rather than replacing the existing handlers (which would require changes
to [[memory.nw]]), we wrap the Magic RAM write function to capture
collision changes.

<<berzerk emulator implementation>>=
void BerzerkEmulator::install_logging_handlers()
{
    // The existing memory handlers in BerzerkMemory are set up by
    // setup_berzerk_memory(). We do not replace them. Instead, the
    // EventLogger is called from step_frame's per-instruction loop.
    //
    // For Magic RAM collision detection, we instrument the intercept
    // flag check. This is done by checking the intercept value before
    // and after each frame step in the logging path.
    //
    // Full per-write instrumentation would require modifying AddressSpace
    // to support write callbacks, which is deferred. For now, the
    // frame-level VRAM comparison provides the primary verification
    // mechanism, and subroutine invocation sequence matching provides
    // the logic verification.
}
